==Latin==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|la|grc|ἀμφορεύς||vased shaped ornament with a narrow neck, literally two-handled pitcher}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|amphora}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|amphora|amphorae|f|first}}

# A [[vessel]], usually [[made]] of [[clay]], with two [[handles]] or [[ears]] for [[liquids]]; [[amphora#English|amphora]]; [[flagon]], [[pitcher]], [[flask]], [[bottle]], [[jar]].
# A [[measure]] for liquids; [[quadrantal]]; the measure of a [[ship]].

====Inflection====
The genitive plural [[amphorarum|amphorārum]] has the alternative form [[amphorum|amphorūm]] which is especially used in the sense of a measure.
{{la-decl-1st|amphor}}

